    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95-a3">

                <pb facs="0279" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v11/pg253"/>


                <head>Memorandum From the Secretary of State to the Legal Adviser (Becker)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1957-10-07">October 7, 1957</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Collective Security Project</item>
                </list>
                <p>I have read your memorandum of October 3, commenting on my memorandum of
                    September 29,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d95-f1"/> on the above subject.</p>
                <p>I suggest as a next step that you form a working group under your chairmanship to
                    explore and develop the concepts put forward in the two memoranda. I would
                    suggest that this working group be <pb facs="0280" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/>
                    composed, in addition to yourself, of a representative from IO,S/P, EUR, FE, ARA
                    and NEA.</p>
                <p>This project should be treated as tentative and highly confidential.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">John Foster Dulles</hi><anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d95-f2"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
